Per-File Attribution Convention
================================

Any source file in this project that adapts, ports, or derives logic from the
above third-party projects carries a header comment block in the following form:

    # Attribution: adapted from <project> (<license>)
    # Upstream file: <upstream/path/to/file.py>
    # Copyright: <copyright holder>
    # Changes: <brief description of modifications>

Example (for a file adapting aider's editblock logic under Apache-2.0):

    # Attribution: adapted from aider (Apache-2.0)
    # Upstream file: aider/coders/editblock_coder.py
    # Copyright: (c) Paul Gauthier and contributors
    # Changes: refactored into Protocol-based strategy, added HunkResult VO,
    #          removed REPL-specific output, integrated with SandboxProvider

Example (for a file adapting hermes's patch parser under MIT):

    # Attribution: adapted from hermes (MIT)
    # Upstream file: hermes/patch_parser.py
    # Copyright: (c) Nous Research and contributors
    # Changes: rewritten as async EditStrategy, integrated with PathLock,
    #          transactional dry-run added

Files that implement ideas inspired by a project but contain NO copied or
directly ported code carry no attribution header (independent reimplementation
requires no notice beyond this NOTICE file).
